---
name: menu-loader
description: Guide for creating and editing .menu.yaml files that define dynamic VS Code menus. Covers the YAML schema, action types (command, shell, snippet, url, chat, clipboard), when-clauses, menu location IDs, and developer tools for command discovery and validation. Use when the user wants to add, edit, or debug custom menus defined in YAML.
---

The **menu-loader** extension scans `.menu.yaml` files from `~/.vscode/menus/` (global) and `.vscode/menus/` (per-workspace) and builds live VS Code menus at runtime. Read the companion reference files before writing YAML:

- **[YAML-FORMAT.md](.github/skills/menu-loader/YAML-FORMAT.md)** — complete schema, every field, every action type
- **[SAMPLES.md](.github/skills/menu-loader/SAMPLES.md)** — annotated examples covering all patterns

---

## Workflow for Creating a New Menu

### 1. Discover what you need

Before writing YAML, gather context using the built-in developer tools.

#### List available commands
Run **"Menu Loader: List All Commands"** (`menuLoader.listCommands`) from the Command Palette. This opens a markdown document listing every registered command grouped by source extension, with command IDs and titles. Use this to find the exact command IDs to put in your YAML.

#### List menu location IDs
Run **"Menu Loader: List Menu Location IDs"** (`menuLoader.listMenuIds`). This shows all known `menu:` values (where your menu will appear) organized by category — Menu Bar, Editor, Explorer, SCM, Terminal, Debug, Notebook, Chat, Views, Global, etc.

#### Inspect existing menus
Run **"Menu Loader: Show Menu Tree"** (`menuLoader.showMenuTree`). This renders all currently loaded `.menu.yaml` files as a Unicode box-drawing tree, showing the hierarchy, when-conditions, and action types at a glance.

### 2. Write the YAML file

Create a `.menu.yaml` file in `.vscode/menus/` (project-local) or `~/.vscode/menus/` (global). See [YAML-FORMAT.md](.github/skills/menu-loader/YAML-FORMAT.md) for the full schema. Minimal example:

```yaml
name: my-menu
menu: MenubarMainMenu
title: My Menu

items:
  - group: 1_main
    items:
      - title: Do Something
        command: myExtension.doSomething
```

### 3. Validate

Run **"Menu Loader: Validate Menu Files"** (`menuLoader.validateMenus`). This checks all loaded `.menu.yaml` files for:
- Missing required fields (`name`, `menu`)
- Unknown menu location IDs
- Command IDs that are not currently registered
- `hasExtension()` references to extensions that are not installed
- Leaf items with no `title`
- Nodes with no action and no children

Fix any issues reported, then reload.

### 4. Reload

Run **"Menu Loader: Reload Menus"** (`menuLoader.reload`) or save the file (the extension watches for changes automatically with a 300ms debounce).

---

## Developer Tool Commands Reference

| Command | ID | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| **List All Commands** | `menuLoader.listCommands` | Dump every registered command to a markdown document, grouped by extension. Use to discover command IDs for the `command:` field. |
| **Show Menu Tree** | `menuLoader.showMenuTree` | Visualize all loaded `.menu.yaml` files as an indented tree with annotations. Use to review structure before editing. |
| **Validate Menu Files** | `menuLoader.validateMenus` | Check all `.menu.yaml` files for structural errors, unknown commands, missing extensions. Run after editing. |
| **List Menu Location IDs** | `menuLoader.listMenuIds` | Show all known menu IDs with descriptions. Use to choose the right `menu:` value. |
| **Reload Menus** | `menuLoader.reload` | Force re-scan and rebuild all menus from YAML files. |

All tools output to an untitled markdown editor — no files are written to disk.

---

## Key Design Patterns

### When-clauses
Every level of the tree (`MenuDefinitionYaml`, groups, items) supports a `when` field. The runtime evaluates these against the current editor context. Common patterns:

| Pattern | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `editorLangId == markdown` | Active editor is Markdown |
| `resourceExtname == .ts` | Active file has `.ts` extension |
| `hasExtension(publisher.name)` | A specific extension is installed |
| `workspaceContains(**/*.py)` | Workspace has Python files |
| `isWindows` / `isMac` / `isLinux` | Platform check |
| `editorHasSelection` | Text is selected in editor |
| `configValue(editor.wordWrap) == on` | A setting has a specific value |

Combine with `&&`, `||`, `!`: `editorLangId == markdown && hasExtension(yzhang.markdown-all-in-one)`

### Six action types (mutually exclusive per leaf item)

| Field | Runs | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `command` | A VS Code command | `command: editor.action.formatDocument` |
| `shell` | A terminal command | `shell: "npm run build"` |
| `snippet` | Inserts a snippet | `snippet: "**${TM_SELECTED_TEXT}**"` |
| `url` | Opens a browser URL | `url: "https://example.com"` |
| `chat` | Opens Copilot Chat | `chat: "Explain this code"` |
| `clipboard` | Copies text to clipboard | `clipboard: "${file}"` |

### Variable expansion
Action values support `${variable}` placeholders resolved at execution time:
`${workspaceFolder}`, `${workspaceFolderBasename}`, `${file}`, `${fileBasename}`, `${fileDirname}`, `${fileExtname}`, `${selectedText}`, `${lineNumber}`, `${clipboard}`, `${env:NAME}`

### Menu locations (most common)
- `MenubarMainMenu` — create a **new** top-level dropdown
- `MenubarFileMenu`, `MenubarEditMenu`, etc. — inject into an **existing** menu
- `EditorContext` — editor right-click menu
- `ExplorerContext` — file explorer right-click
- `window/toolbar` — toolbar strip (proposed API)

Run `menuLoader.listMenuIds` for the full list with descriptions.

### Tree structure
```
MenuDefinitionYaml          ← top-level: name, menu, title, when, items
  └── items[]               ← array of MenuNodeYaml
        ├── group node      ← has group + items[], creates separator section (depth 0) or submenu (depth > 0)
        ├── submenu node    ← has title + items[], no action
        └── leaf node       ← has title + exactly one action field
```

---

## Common Mistakes

1. **Wrong menu ID** — Use `MenubarMainMenu` (not `MainMenu`, not `menubar`). Run `menuLoader.listMenuIds` to check.
2. **Multiple actions on one item** — Each leaf must have exactly ONE of: `command`, `shell`, `snippet`, `url`, `chat`, `clipboard`.
3. **Missing `name` or `menu`** — Both are required at the top level. `name` is the internal identifier; `menu` is where it appears.
4. **Command not showing up** — The extension owning the command may not have activated. Use `when: "hasExtension(publisher.name)"` to guard conditional items.
5. **Forgetting `title` on leaf items** — Without `title`, the raw command ID is used as the label.
6. **YAML indentation** — Use consistent 2-space indentation. Items must be nested under their parent's `items:` key.

---

## Iterating with the Tools

The recommended edit cycle:

1. Run `menuLoader.listCommands` → find command IDs you want
2. Run `menuLoader.listMenuIds` → pick the right `menu:` target
3. Write or edit the `.menu.yaml` file
4. Run `menuLoader.validateMenus` → fix any issues
5. Run `menuLoader.showMenuTree` → verify the structure looks right
6. The menu auto-reloads on file save (or run `menuLoader.reload`)
